     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Cabrera-Walton Clinic\nPatient: Anthony Reed DOB: 07/15/1960 Sex: M MRN: 701653\n\nEncounters:\n 2024-11-22 Cancer (see type table) BP 147/83 Wt 149\n 2024-08-08 Cancer (see type table) BP 141/91 Wt 148\n 2024-04-24 lab review BP 153/94 Wt 156\n 2024-01-09 Cancer (see type table) BP 150/88 Wt 149\n 2023-09-25 Cancer (see type table) BP 149/84 Wt 158\n 2023-06-11 rash BP 153/90 Wt 150\n 2023-02-25 Cancer (see type table) BP 152/86 Wt 143\n 2022-11-11 lab review BP 153/91 Wt 144\n 2022-07-28 Cancer (see type table) BP 149/89 Wt 144\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Melanoma cancer, stage II (s/p treatment ~24.3 years ago) - controlled; meds: none\n - The patient has a controlled stage II melanoma, having completed treatment approximately 24.3 years ago. There are no current signs of recurrence. The patient continues to be monitored with periodic follow-ups and lab assessments.\n • Hypertension - managed\n - The patient's blood pressure readings have ranged from 141/91 mmHg to 153/94 mmHg across various visits. Antihypertensive medications are currently not prescribed, but lifestyle modifications and continued monitoring are recommended.\n • Rash evaluation\n - On June 11, 2023, the patient presented with a rash. After evaluation, the cause was determined to be non-specific, and no specific treatment was needed. The rash has since resolved.\n • Tobacco use\n - The patient is an active smoker, consuming one pack of cigarettes per day. He started smoking in February 1980 and has not attempted to quit. Counseling on the risks of continued smoking and resources for cessation have been provided.\n • Alcohol consumption\n - The patient reports consuming approximately 12 drinks per week. This level of alcohol use does not currently meet criteria for intervention, but the patient has been advised on the potential health risks associated with alcohol consumption.\n • Family history\n - The patient's mother had a myocardial infarction at the age of 68 and passed away at the age of 82. There is no history of hereditary cancer syndromes in the family.\n\nVitals Summary:\n - Blood Pressure:\n - November 22, 2024: 147/83 mmHg\n - August 8, 2024: 141/91 mmHg\n - April 24, 2024: 153/94 mmHg\n - January 9, 2024: 150/88 mmHg\n - September 25, 2023: 149/84 mmHg\n - June 11, 2023: 153/90 mmHg\n - February 25, 2023: 152/86 mmHg\n - November 11, 2022: 153/91 mmHg\n - July 28, 2022: 149/89 mmHg\n - Weight:\n - November 22, 2024: 149 lbs\n - August 8, 2024: 148 lbs\n - April 24, 2024: 156 lbs\n - January 9, 2"
