     "text": "024: 149 lbs\n - September 25, 2023: 158 lbs\n - June 11, 2023: 150 lbs\n - February 25, 2023: 143 lbs\n - November 11, 2022: 144 lbs\n - July 28, 2022: 144 lbs\n\nAdditional Findings:\n - Physical examination on the last visit was within normal limits, with no signs of metastatic disease. The patient's cardiovascular, respiratory, and gastrointestinal exams were unremarkable. Musculoskeletal exam showed no abnormalities, and neurological examination was non-focal.\n - Lab results the most recent visits have shown stable renal and hepatic function, with no significant abnormalities noted.\n - The patient reports occasional headaches, which have not been severe enough to warrant specific treatment. These are likely related to stress and not indicative of any underlying condition.\n\nFollow-Up:\n - The patient is scheduled for routine follow-up visits every 3-6 months to monitor his melanoma status and manage any other health concerns. Regular blood pressure monitoring and weight tracking are advised. Further evaluation and treatment will be initiated if any new symptoms or abnormalities arise.\n\nDr. Jodi Bray, MD, Oncology\nCabrera-Walton Clinic\n\n---\n\nThis clinical summary provides a comprehensive overview of Anthony Reed's medical history, current health status, and ongoing management plan. The data presented is accurate and up-to-date, reflecting the patient's most recent encounters and assessments. This summary is intended for use by healthcare providers and life insurance underwriters to assess the patient's health and risk profile comprehensively.\n"
